  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "The researcher Chris Ramsay says that a remote viewer named Joe McMoneagle would go into a SCIF, a sealed room for handling classified material, and do remote viewing, which means trying to describe distant places or things using only the mind. He did this each year so the budget of Stargate, a US government programme that studied remote viewing, would be renewed. Ramsay tells this without naming a source, and if true it would mean officials kept paying because the demonstrations convinced them."
